#: ../../../governance.md:1
msgid "Governance"
msgstr "治理"

#: ../../../governance.md:3
msgid ""
"The Gazebo project, a project under the Open Source Robotics Foundation, is "
"managed by the Open Source Robotics Alliance (OSRA). The OSRA-appointed "
"Technical Governance Committee provides oversight of the project, while the "
"Project Management Committee is responsible for day-to-day operations. This "
"document outlines these entities and their respective roles and "
"responsibilities. For further information, please refer to [OSRA website]"
"(https://osralliance.org/how-it-works/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../governance.md:11
msgid "Open Source Robotics Alliance (OSRA)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../governance.md:13
msgid ""
"The Open Source Robotics Foundation (OSRF) established the Open Source "
"Robotics Alliance (OSRA) to enhance the governance of its open-source "
"projects including Gazebo. Inspired by the success of organizations like The "
"Linux Foundation and the Eclipse Foundation, OSRA aims to provide funding, "
"encourage greater community involvement, and ensure the long-term stability "
"of these projects. The OSRA has a Technical Governance Committee that "
"oversees the technical aspects of the projects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../governance.md:21
msgid "Technical Governance Committee (TGC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../governance.md:23
msgid ""
"The TGC provides guidance and oversight to each of the projects. Its "
"responsibilities include approving proposed activities of each Project "
"Management Committee (PMC), approving Project Leader nominations, and "
"reporting to the OSRF Board on the activities of the OSRA and status of each "
"project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../governance.md:28
msgid "Gazebo PMC Meetings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../governance.md:30
msgid ""
"Community members are encouraged to *observe* the Gazebo PMC meetings and "
"submit agenda items via a PMC constituent. To add an item to the Gazebo PMC "
"agenda please contact one of the PMC constituents list below. Gazebo PMC "
"meetings are conducted using Zoom and presently occur every Monday. To join "
"the Gazebo PMC meeting please use the [link available in our official OSRA "
"Google calendar](https://calendar.google.com/calendar/u/0/embed?"
"src=agf3kajirket8khktupm9go748@group.calendar.google.com&ctz=Etc%2FUTC)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../governance.md:35
msgid "The Gazebo Project Management Committee (PMC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../governance.md:37
msgid ""
"The Gazebo PMC is responsible for the day-to-day management of the Gazebo "
"project including setting the project’s roadmap, coordinating development "
"activities from individual contributors, and facilitating community "
"engagement. The PMC is also responsible for electing the Project Leader and "
"approving PMC member and committer nominations. The PMC consists of the "
"Project Leader, Members (individuals with full voting rights), a Supporting "
"Individual Representative, and the Chair of the TGC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../governance.md:45
msgid "Committers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../governance.md:47
msgid ""
"The Gazebo project also has committers. These are individuals who have "
"commit access to one or more of the Gazebo repositories and help the PMC "
"maintain the project by contributing code, reviewing pull requests, and "
"responding to issues, etc. While committers typically don't have voting "
"rights within the PMC and aren't considered PMC members, it's possible to "
"hold both roles. Conversely, all PMC members are required to be committers."
msgstr ""

